  <bib:Article rdf:about="#reflectiverag_verma">
    <z:itemType>conferencePaper</z:itemType>
    <dc:title>ReflectiveRAG: Rethinking Adaptivity in Retrieval-Augmented Generation</dc:title>
    <dc:date>2026</dc:date>
    <z:url>https://aclanthology.org/2026.eacl-industry.27/</z:url>
    <dc:identifier>DOI: 10.18653/v1/2026.eacl-industry.27</dc:identifier>
    <z:extra>发表状态：已同行评审，EACL 2026 Industry Track；不是主会 Long。阅读优先级：P0-强基线。引用快照：Semantic Scholar 2；OpenAlex 1（2026-08-13，论文很新）。为什么读：它是 fresh per-query repair 的最直接正式基线：先判断证据充分性，再迭代 query reformulation，且不训练策略。精读问题：何时判定不足？fresh repair 的真实调用、token、延迟是多少？我们的 REUSE 若仍调用同等规模 LLM，是否真的节约成本？</z:extra>
    <bib:authors><rdf:Seq>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Akshay</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Verma</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Swapnil</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Gupta</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Siddharth</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Pillai</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Prateek</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Sircar</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Deepak</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Gupta</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
    </rdf:Seq></bib:authors>
    <dcterms:isPartOf><bib:Proceedings><dc:title>Proceedings of EACL 2026 (Volume 5: Industry Track)</dc:title></bib:Proceedings></dcterms:isPartOf>
    <z:tags><rdf:Bag><rdf:li><z:AutomaticTag><rdf:value>GrowRAG-核心精读</rdf:value></z:AutomaticTag></rdf:li><rdf:li><z:AutomaticTag><rdf:value>P0-Fresh-Repair基线</rdf:value></z:AutomaticTag></rdf:li><rdf:li><z:AutomaticTag><rdf:value>同行评审-Industry</rdf:value></z:AutomaticTag></rdf:li></rdf:Bag></z:tags>
  </bib:Article>

  <bib:Article rdf:about="#s2grag">
    <z:itemType>conferencePaper</z:itemType>
    <dc:title>S2G-RAG: Structured Sufficiency and Gap Judging for Iterative Retrieval-Augmented QA</dc:title>
    <dc:date>2026</dc:date>
    <z:url>https://aclanthology.org/2026.acl-long.1185/</z:url>
    <dc:identifier>DOI: 10.18653/v1/2026.acl-long.1185</dc:identifier>
    <z:extra>发表状态：已同行评审，ACL 2026 Long。阅读优先级：P0-强基线。引用快照：OpenAlex 0（2026-08-13，论文很新）。为什么读：它把证据充分性和缺口判断结构化，可帮助定义 reactive repair 的触发器。精读问题：sufficiency 与 gap 如何标注/推断？它解决的是本题内检索循环，还是跨题经验？</z:extra>
